(Chapter One: The Lighthouse) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
0 -28 Td
15 TL
(Maren took the ferry to the island on the first morning of spring.) Tj T*
(The lighthouse keeper had retired in winter, and nobody had replaced him.) Tj T*
(She found the logbook open on the desk, its last entry dated the night of the storm.) Tj T*
(Every page recorded the same ritual: trim the wick, wind the clockwork, note the wind.) Tj T*
(By noon she had cleaned the lens and discovered that the clockwork still turned.) Tj T*
(That evening the light swept the bay for the first time in four months.) Tj T*
ET
