(Chapter Two: The Logbook) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
0 -28 Td
15 TL
(The entries grew shorter toward the end, as if the keeper had been saving ink.) Tj T*
(One line mentioned a boat that passed too close to the rocks and never answered the horn.) Tj T*
(Maren compared the dates with the harbor records and found the boat had been reported missing.) Tj T*
(She wrote her own first entry that night, copying the ritual word for word.) Tj T*
(The wind was from the north, the lens was clean, and the light did not fail.) Tj T*
(In the morning she radioed the harbor to say the lighthouse was keeping watch again.) Tj T*
ET
